; square.scm with * expanded, as basic blocks (framing example of the lambda versioning chapter).
; * tests the type of x once (both operands are x). A fixnum x gives a fixnum, or a bignum on
; overflow; a flonum x gives a flonum. Each way of computing x * x returns from its own exit site.
function square(x)
A:  if fixnum?(x) goto B else goto D
B:  y = fx*?(x, x)
    if y goto R else goto C
R:  return y
C:  return ##*(x, x)
D:  if flonum?(x) goto E else goto F
E:  return fl*(x, x)
F:  return ##*(x, x)
